From: well0nez <8986239+well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: arm64: dts: h713: the AV1 decoder stays off for now

The AV1 core shares the video engine's bus. Next to it, the engine's
recovery after a damaged H.265 stream (0308) cannot release the
engine's IOMMU ports without costing the AV1 stream frames or stopping
the SoC (arbeit/medien/B6-mythos, 14.10.2026: every variant tried), so
0308 leaves the ports blocked while an AV1 stream is open. Two decodes
at once are not a use of this device, and the AV1 decoder is not
needed for the media work ahead of it, so it stays off: the node is
disabled here and CONFIG_VIDEO_HANTRO is off in the board defconfig.
The driver, the guard's stream accounting and the measurements stay
in the series; to bring the core back, drop this patch and turn the
option on again, then repeat the gates of packages C and B6 next to
each other (decision: Marco, 14.10.2026).
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
@@ -1509,7 +1509,14 @@
 			allwinner,video-engine = <&ve>;
 			iommus = <&iommu 5 1>;
 			power-domains = <&ppu 4>;
-			status = "okay";
+			/*
+			 * Off for now (14.10.2026): next to a decoding AV1 core
+			 * the engine's recovery after a damaged stream cannot
+			 * release its IOMMU ports (0308), and two decodes at
+			 * once are not a use of this device. "okay" brings the
+			 * core back, together with CONFIG_VIDEO_HANTRO.
+			 */
+			status = "disabled";
 		};
 
 		/* === GPU (Mali-G31 Bifrost, Panfrost driver) === */
